199:Our study has several limitations. First, only age and gender were considered as independent variables to estimate the brain readout in the normative model. Cognitive scores and home environment may also affect the brain index. These covariates also need to be considered for more comprehensive models. Second, although we demonstrated the stability and robustness of the clustering solution in different datasets, we did not /uniFB01 nd any brain-symptom correlations either within or across subtypes. A potential cause is the complex relationship between brain imaging and symptom dimensions, which might not be delineated using straightforward linear strategies. Biologically homogeneous subtypes identi /uniFB01 ed by brain imaging might offer speci /uniFB01 c information of clinical utility, and investigation of the effective interventions suited for different subtypes is greatly needed in future studies. Finally, other modalities, including resting-state functional MRI, diffusion tensor imaging, and genetic data, need to be incorporated to parse the heterogeneity of ASD.
